---
title: Lamb barbacoa tacos
tags: [mexican, lamb, weekend]
cuisine: mexican
time: 6 hours
source: Lamb Barbacoa Taco by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/lamb-barbacoa-taco-2
---

== Dry rub ==

Mix the @pasilla chiles{4}(toasted and ground), @cascabel chiles{2}(toasted and ground), @whole cloves{4}, @coriander seeds{1%tbsp}, @cinnamon sticks{1/2} and @salt{} to taste.

== Lamb ==

Rub the @lamb shanks{3%kg} all over with the dry rub in a #hotel pan{}. Cover and refrigerate ~{2%hours}.

Put the @chickpeas{1%cup}, @carrot{1}(chopped), @chipotle pepper{1}(chopped) and @water{2%l} in the bottom of a #steamer pot{} and set the rack in place.

Line the rack with the @maguey leaf{1}(charred) and half the @avocado leaves{12}. Lay the lamb on top with the @garlic{1%head}(halved), and cover with the rest of the avocado leaves.

Seal with foil and the lid and steam over low heat ~{4%hours}, until the meat is tender. The liquid underneath is the consommé; keep it warm.

== Assembly ==

Lift the lamb out with a slotted spoon and shred it.

Pile the lamb on @corn tortillas{} and top with @cilantro{}(leaves). Serve with @lime wedges{} and a small bowl of the consommé.
